  "description": "The polar bear, known scientifically as Ursus maritimus, is a large carnivorous bear species found in the Arctic region. They are well adapted to life in the cold, with a thick layer of fat and a water-repellent coat that insulates them from the frigid temperatures. Polar bears primarily hunt seals and are known for their excellent swimming abilities, often covering long distances in search of food. They play a crucial role as apex predators in their ecosystem, but their populations are currently threatened by climate change and habitat loss due to melting sea ice.",
